# Copy to .env.gateway and fill in. This file holds secrets — it is gitignored; never commit it.

# --- Your domain, for Caddy's automatic TLS certificate (deploy/Caddyfile) ---
# Use "localhost" to try the gateway locally with a self-signed certificate.
GATEWAY_DOMAIN=gateway.example.com

# --- Model provider: set exactly one pair, pointing at your real provider's API ---
GATEWAY_OPENAI_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
GATEWAY_OPENAI_KEY=

# GATEWAY_ANTHROPIC_URL=https://api.anthropic.com/v1
# GATEWAY_ANTHROPIC_KEY=

# GATEWAY_GEMINI_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta
# GATEWAY_GEMINI_KEY=

# --- Required: turns sensitive values into keyed commitments before they ever reach the signed
#     audit ledger, instead of being written in the clear. Generate your own, don't reuse this:
#       openssl rand -hex 32
GATEWAY_REDACTOR_SECRET=

# --- Advanced (optional) — leave all of this unset for the default: discovery and attacks run,
#     nothing is blocked yet, until you've reviewed the findings and approved a signed policy.
#     See README.md "Turning enforcement on" before setting any of these.
# GATEWAY_ENFORCE=true
# GATEWAY_POLICY_FILE=/var/lib/purpleteam/policy.json
# GATEWAY_POLICY_TRUST_FILE=/var/lib/purpleteam/policy-trust.json

# --- Advanced (optional) — hardware-backed checkpoint signing; needs a TPM (Windows) or a
#     configured PKCS#11/KMS backend. Leave unset if you don't have one.
# GATEWAY_HARDWARE_SIGNING=preferred
# GATEWAY_HARDWARE_BACKEND=tpm
